<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>dev.tensorseed.Tensorseed</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>AGPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>Tensorseed Desktop</name>
  <!-- Desktop does not serve inference yet (the CLI does), so its summary
       leaves serving out. Switch to the main tagline, "Download, seed, and
       serve AI models you can verify", once the Desktop serve control
       ships; keep the .desktop Comment and shortDescription in
       tauri.conf.json the same (a unit test checks). -->
  <summary>Download, seed, and verify AI models</summary>
  <developer id="dev.tensorseed">
    <name>Tuned Chaos</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Tensorseed Desktop browses signed Tensorseed catalogs of open AI models
      and datasets. Each catalog is anchored on the Chia blockchain, so you can
      check that the list of files you are about to download is the one its
      publisher signed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Desktop pulls models over BitTorrent with an HTTP fallback, verifies every
      file against the signed manifest, and seeds verified copies back to other
      users, so a model stays available even when its original host is not.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Search catalogs and open an entry from a tensorseed:// link</li>
      <li>Pull, verify, and seed models and datasets</li>
      <li>Pause, resume, and limit seeding, and keep seeding from the system tray</li>
      <li>Share config, keys, and pulled copies with the tensorseed command line tool</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Serving a verified model through an inference engine such as llama.cpp or
      vLLM is done with the tensorseed command line tool and an engine you
      install separately. Downloading, verifying, and seeding never need one.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">dev.tensorseed.Tensorseed.desktop</launchable>
  <icon type="stock">dev.tensorseed.Tensorseed</icon>
  <provides>
    <binary>tensorseed-desktop</binary>
    <binary>tensorseed</binary>
  </provides>
  <url type="homepage">https://tensorseed.dev</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/TunedChaos/TensorSeed</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/TunedChaos/TensorSeed/issues</url>
